Subject: [PATCH 6/6] sr-aef: name an unnamed glyph as fontTools does

A glyph a font leaves unnamed (post format 3, or an empty post name) took
skrifa's made-up name, "gid94"; fontTools calls it "glyph00094", and glyph 0
".notdef". Tools that pair a converted font's glyphs with the binary's by name
then miss them: six of Lato's unnamed glyphs, same outline and advance, found
no counterpart. An unnamed glyph is now ".notdef" if it is glyph 0 and
otherwise "glyph" and its five-digit glyph id, as fontTools names a glyph that
no cmap entry names (an encoded one it names for its codepoint, which is left
to the converter). Test: resources/noname.ttf (make_noname.py).

Assisted by an AI agent (Claude Opus 5.5)
